let me know you are here.

150
00:12:47,472 --> 00:12:50,672
I actually tried to say hello earlier, but...

151
00:12:50,672 --> 00:12:52,472
The fire...

152
00:12:53,438 --> 00:12:55,405
There's a fire!

153
00:12:56,938 --> 00:12:59,705
Wait, wait, it's dangerous!
Don't get close. Hold on, hold on.

154
00:12:59,705 --> 00:13:01,638
Wait, what is this?

155
00:13:01,638 --> 00:13:04,338
W-What did you put in it?

156
00:13:20,138 --> 00:13:21,772
Here, here!

157
00:13:22,972 --> 00:13:26,205
When you put out this kind of fire,
you have to cut off the oxygen first.

158
00:13:35,672 --> 00:13:37,272
What is this?

159
00:13:50,405 --> 00:13:52,372
That could've been bad.

160
00:13:53,338 --> 00:13:54,972
Thank you.

161
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:01,538
Where exactly were you
trying to aim the extinguisher?

162
00:14:15,872 --> 00:14:17,838
It's okay now.

163
00:14:20,472 --> 00:14:24,005
I know this isn't really my place, but...

164
00:14:24,838 --> 00:14:28,838
Min Seo's father is a parent too.

165
00:14:28,838 --> 00:14:32,105
How can he use his own child
as a bargaining chip?

166
00:14:32,105 --> 00:14:34,305
Seriously.

167
00:14:34,305 --> 00:14:37,372
In a case like this, you should just
take it all the way to court, you know?

168
00:14:37,372 --> 00:14:40,572
You have to fight tooth and nail
and take him for everything he's got.

169
00:14:40,572 --> 00:14:44,772
Thank you, I'll take him
for everything he's got.

170
00:14:45,938 --> 00:14:47,505
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

171
00:14:47,505 --> 00:14:48,672
Hello, yeah.

172
00:14:48,672 --> 00:14:50,172
This is my senior actor, Kang Tae Han.

173
00:14:50,172 --> 00:14:51,772
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you. I'm Kang Tae Han.

174
00:14:51,772 --> 00:14:55,438
Yes, I've really enjoyed your work.
Nice to meet you.

175
00:14:57,238 --> 00:15:00,372
After you're done with your appointment,
could we maybe take a photo...

176
00:15:00,372 --> 00:15:01,872
- A picture? Sure, anytime.
- Is that okay?

177
00:15:01,872 --> 00:15:04,038
- Of course. I'd be happy to.
- Thank you.

178
00:15:04,038 --> 00:15:05,672
I'll take a selfie for you.

179
00:15:05,672 --> 00:15:06,738
One, two...

180
00:15:06,738 --> 00:15:08,572
- Hello.
- Hello.

181
00:15:08,572 --> 00:15:09,972
Oh, this is mine.

182
00:15:09,972 --> 00:15:11,472
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

183
00:15:11,472 --> 00:15:14,572
This is mine, so I'll send it
to you after we're done.

184
00:15:14,572 --> 00:15:16,538
- This is my senior actor, Kang Tae Han.
- Oh, yes.

185
00:15:16,538 --> 00:15:17,638
- Hello, I'm Kang Tae Han.
- This is the director.

186
00:15:17,638 --> 00:15:19,438
- Oh, Director.
- Hello.

187
00:15:20,672 --> 00:15:22,872
Then we can take the picture later,
after we're done, right?

188
00:15:22,872 --> 00:15:24,505
Yes.

189
00:15:42,372 --> 00:15:44,338
[@Chastaryobb_ Love today's outfit]

190
00:16:47,705 --> 00:16:51,905
Wow, this is really neat.

191
00:16:51,905 --> 00:16:57,338
Anyway, you two look so happy together.

192
00:16:57,338 --> 00:17:00,105
But aren't you a little worried?

193
00:17:00,105 --> 00:17:03,438
I saw at the hospital
that your husband is still very popular.

194
00:17:03,438 --> 00:17:07,138
- Oh, not at all.
- It's good if an actor is popular.

195
00:17:07,138 --> 00:17:12,005
Even Ms. Ryu Ji Su calls him oppa
and is naturally touchy-feely.

196
00:17:12,805 --> 00:17:15,405
Oh my, be careful.

197
00:17:15,405 --> 00:17:17,638
Oh, what do I do? I'm sorry.
Did it splash on this thing?

198
00:17:17,638 --> 00:17:19,038
The furniture is fine.

199
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:21,738
Your clothes got stained though.
Go clean it up quickly.

200
00:17:21,738 --> 00:17:24,405
- It's all over your clothes.
- It's fine. Are you okay?

201
00:17:24,405 --> 00:17:25,972
- Yeah, I'm fine.
- Oh, jeez...

202
00:17:25,972 --> 00:17:27,505
- Where can I find...
- Down the hall

203
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:29,205
- Oh, yes.
- at the end.

204
00:17:29,205 --> 00:17:31,705
Oh, what a mess.

205
00:17:31,705 --> 00:17:33,872
- Are you okay?
- What? Oh, I...

206
00:17:33,872 --> 00:17:36,072
Be careful.

207
00:17:36,072 --> 00:17:37,305
- I'll...
- Please be careful.

208
00:17:37,305 --> 00:17:38,938
Yeah.

209
00:17:40,238 --> 00:17:44,272
Something always happens
whenever we meet, doesn't it?

210
00:17:45,638 --> 00:17:47,305
I know, right?

211
00:17:48,205 --> 00:17:53,338
At this rate, are we going to
have a car accident next time?

212
00:17:59,772 --> 00:18:02,272
- Oh my, you're bleeding here.
- What?

213
00:18:03,538 --> 00:18:05,972
- I'm fine.
- Would you like to go to the guest room?

214
00:18:05,972 --> 00:18:07,405
There's a first-aid kit there.

215
00:18:07,405 --> 00:18:11,372
It's not a deep cut,
but it could still get infected.

216
00:18:12,305 --> 00:18:14,272
Oh, really?

217
00:18:17,672 --> 00:18:19,705
It might sting a little.

218
00:18:49,005 --> 00:18:51,872
I-I still need to finish the dressing...

219
00:18:51,872 --> 00:18:55,105
Yeah, you should dress it.

220
00:19:10,705 --> 00:19:12,605
- Are you okay?
- What?

221
00:19:12,605 --> 00:19:13,638
Huh?

222
00:19:13,638 --> 00:19:15,638
- Why are you coming out from there?
- Oh.

223
00:19:15,638 --> 00:19:17,438
I cut my hand earlier.

224
00:19:17,438 --> 00:19:19,272
Jeez, let me see.

225
00:19:21,505 --> 00:19:23,605
It's fine.

226
00:19:23,605 --> 00:19:25,738
- Look at this bandage job.
- The bandage is all crumpled.

227
00:19:25,738 --> 00:19:27,272
That's a pretty deep cut. Huh?

228
00:19:27,272 --> 00:19:28,938
It's done now.

229
00:19:30,238 --> 00:19:31,772
Oh, right.

230
00:19:31,772 --> 00:19:37,238
I'll arrange a meeting with Aunt Michelle.

231
00:19:40,205 --> 00:19:43,972
We should help each other out.
We're neighbors, after all.

232
00:19:46,238 --> 00:19:49,872
[Autonomous driving mode]

233
00:19:53,905 --> 00:19:55,605
[Please take control of the steering wheel]

234
00:20:05,272 --> 00:20:07,705
We almost ended up dead.

235
00:20:07,705 --> 00:20:09,638
That startled me.

236
00:20:11,072 --> 00:20:13,172
Oh, honey.

237
00:20:13,172 --> 00:20:15,105
That was dangerous.

238
00:20:35,472 --> 00:20:36,538
[Are things going well with Aunt Michelle?]

239
00:20:36,538 --> 00:20:37,738
[No, she's still not here]

240
00:20:37,738 --> 00:20:38,738
[Really? She's not the type to be late]

241
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:40,372
[I miss you]

242
00:20:48,872 --> 00:20:50,672
Min Seo!

243
00:20:50,672 --> 00:20:52,438
What are you doing there?

244
00:20:58,272 --> 00:21:01,372
Why? Are you going to tear it up again?

245
00:21:04,772 --> 00:21:06,742
[It would be nice if we could eat together.]

246
00:21:06,742 --> 00:21:07,975
[Actually, what I really want is...]

247
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,205
[You know it's you, right?]

248
00:21:13,972 --> 00:21:16,605
It's still chilly out here.

249
00:21:16,605 --> 00:21:18,472
Go inside and draw.

250
00:21:33,372 --> 00:21:34,372
[Courtroom 416, Court in Session]

251
00:21:34,372 --> 00:21:37,105
Today is just a formality
to confirm a few things.

252
00:21:37,105 --> 00:21:40,272
Oh, hello. It's been a while.

253
00:21:40,272 --> 00:21:44,838
Hello, I'm Choi Sang Cheol,
the attorney representing your husband.

254
00:21:44,838 --> 00:21:47,038
Oh, I see.

255
00:21:49,872 --> 00:21:52,005
This is going to be a headache.

256
00:21:52,005 --> 00:21:53,372
Why?

257
00:21:53,372 --> 00:21:56,172
Just, for someone who calls himself a lawyer,

258
00:21:56,172 --> 00:21:59,472
he's always pulling stunts
outside the courtroom.

259
00:22:00,205 --> 00:22:01,438
You are here.

260
00:22:01,438 --> 00:22:02,705
You came early.

261
00:22:02,705 --> 00:22:04,705
Traffic was bad.

262
00:22:05,338 --> 00:22:08,772
As I mentioned,
this shouldn't take too long today.

263
00:22:11,505 --> 00:22:14,138
- I'm worried.
- About what?

264
00:22:14,138 --> 00:22:17,972
I asked around,
and turns out, this Choi Sang Cheol thinks

265
00:22:17,972 --> 00:22:20,472
illegal recording and stalking
are just part of the job.

266
00:22:20,472 --> 00:22:23,872
He's not a lawyer.
He's nothing but a lowlife thug.

267
00:22:23,872 --> 00:22:25,338
Yeah?

268
00:22:25,338 --> 00:22:27,638
Then you need to fight back just as hard.

269
00:22:27,638 --> 00:22:29,738
People like that...

270
00:22:32,005 --> 00:22:35,205
Oh, honey, should I introduce you
to a private investigator?

271
00:22:35,972 --> 00:22:37,538
I don't think I need to go that far.

272
00:22:37,538 --> 00:22:40,905
I mean, you said he cheated on you

273
00:22:40,905 --> 00:22:43,072
more than once
when you two were living together.

274
00:22:43,072 --> 00:22:47,838
So if we dig into his background a little,
don't you think we'll find something?

275
00:22:47,838 --> 00:22:50,072
- You know Park & Jeong, right?
- Yeah.

276
00:22:50,072 --> 00:22:53,605
They're one of the top divorce law firms.

277
00:22:53,605 --> 00:22:55,405
You know, when our CEO got divorced,

278
00:22:55,405 --> 00:22:59,572
she trusted their reputation
and handed everything over to them.

279
00:22:59,572 --> 00:23:04,072
And she almost lost everything,
the Cheongnam apartment, her son, everything.

280
00:23:04,072 --> 00:23:06,172
In the end, out of desperation,

281
00:23:06,172 --> 00:23:09,338
she hired a private investigator
as a last resort...

282
00:23:09,338 --> 00:23:11,238
- Oh, it's hot!
- Sorry, sorry.

283
00:23:11,238 --> 00:23:12,838
Is it hot?

284
00:23:15,538 --> 00:23:17,572
- Are you alright?
- Yeah.

285
00:23:18,338 --> 00:23:21,038
Anyway, she hired
a private investigator back then

286
00:23:21,038 --> 00:23:23,905
and had them quietly look into her husband.

287
00:23:23,905 --> 00:23:26,938
And just like that,
everything was taken care of in one go.

288
00:23:28,238 --> 00:23:31,872
What do you think?
Should I get you the number?

289
00:23:33,072 --> 00:23:35,538
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

290
00:23:35,538 --> 00:23:38,405
You're probably stressed enough
because of those rumors.

291
00:23:38,405 --> 00:23:40,538
Yeah, tell me about it.

292
00:23:41,272 --> 00:23:44,505
I mean, how did I end up in a scandal
with Ryu Ji Su? It's ridiculous.

293
00:23:44,505 --> 00:23:46,172
You're right.

294
00:23:48,138 --> 00:23:49,538
All done?

295
00:23:49,538 --> 00:23:51,305
You look pretty.

296
00:24:22,172 --> 00:24:25,105
I like this part.

297
00:24:25,105 --> 00:24:28,005
Who is this? Liv? Jenny?

298
00:24:28,005 --> 00:24:30,538
It's not Jenny, it's Jenna.

299
00:24:30,538 --> 00:24:32,172
Oh...

300
00:24:33,838 --> 00:24:35,772
<i>You've got a message.</i>

301
00:24:40,605 --> 00:24:43,638
Mom, do you need money?

302
00:24:43,638 --> 00:24:46,238
Huh? Why do you ask?

303
00:24:46,238 --> 00:24:48,205
Because you've been using
Gogo Used Market a lot lately.

304
00:24:48,205 --> 00:24:51,072
Oh, no, no.

305
00:24:51,072 --> 00:24:52,738
That's not it.

306
00:24:52,738 --> 00:24:56,005
Your ring is pretty. Did Dad give it to you?

307
00:24:57,138 --> 00:24:58,805
Yeah.

308
00:25:14,005 --> 00:25:16,938
Mom, has something good happened lately?

309
00:25:17,672 --> 00:25:19,238
No, why?

310
00:25:19,238 --> 00:25:22,005
You just seem happier these days.

311
00:25:22,005 --> 00:25:25,472
Oh, no, it's just that...

312
00:25:25,472 --> 00:25:28,305
You have seemed happier lately

313
00:25:28,305 --> 00:25:32,105
and seeing that makes me happy too, Min Seo.

314
00:25:45,172 --> 00:25:47,372
[Lim Ye Ji: Min Seo, is something
going on at your house?]

315
00:25:47,372 --> 00:25:49,938
[Right now, in front of your house...]

316
00:25:52,105 --> 00:25:54,672
Huh? What is it?

317
00:25:55,705 --> 00:25:57,972
Huh? Wait...

318
00:25:57,972 --> 00:25:59,938
Why are there so many police officers here?

319
00:26:13,305 --> 00:26:15,472
She said she wants to die.
The girl said she wants to die.

320
00:26:15,472 --> 00:26:17,705
If this isn't abuse, then what is?

321
00:26:21,405 --> 00:26:22,472
Come quickly. Hurry.

322
00:26:22,472 --> 00:26:25,105
She's a child abuser.
Please arrest her quickly.

323
00:26:25,105 --> 00:26:26,272
Please separate them. Quickly.

324
00:26:26,272 --> 00:26:28,405
Now, wait, just a moment.

325
00:26:28,405 --> 00:26:29,772
Are you saying it's child abuse?

326
00:26:29,772 --> 00:26:31,138
How shameless.

327
00:26:31,138 --> 00:26:33,705
Sir, please calm down.

328
00:26:33,705 --> 00:26:36,472
Could we speak with Min Seo first?

329
00:26:36,472 --> 00:26:38,805
We just need to ask her a few questions.

330
00:26:40,805 --> 00:26:42,472
Wait...

331
00:26:56,338 --> 00:26:57,672
Did you go to your dad again?

332
00:26:57,672 --> 00:27:00,405
Why didn't you tell me?

333
00:27:00,405 --> 00:27:03,038
Mom, I...

334
00:27:03,038 --> 00:27:05,538
You should've told me yourself.

335
00:27:05,538 --> 00:27:07,881
That I monitor you, tear up your drawings,

336
00:27:07,881 --> 00:27:10,372
and make you so suffocated you wanna die...

337
00:27:10,372 --> 00:27:14,105
You didn't have to make them all hear this.

338
00:27:14,105 --> 00:27:18,905
That's... I didn't even know
Dad was recording.

339
00:27:18,905 --> 00:27:22,072
I never thought he'd use my words like this.

340
00:27:22,072 --> 00:27:24,272
But I told the police it was all in the past

341
00:27:24,272 --> 00:27:26,438
and that things are okay now.

342
00:27:26,438 --> 00:27:30,872
- It'll be okay.
- It's not okay at all, Min Seo! This...

343
00:27:30,872 --> 00:27:33,005
What else did you tell your Dad about me?

344
00:27:33,005 --> 00:27:35,738
What did you hand over to that lawyer
that made him so sure of himself,

345
00:27:35,738 --> 00:27:37,638
claiming he has tons of evidence of abuse?

346
00:27:37,638 --> 00:27:39,505
Huh? Min Seo...

347
00:27:50,338 --> 00:27:52,438
Alright.

348
00:27:52,438 --> 00:27:54,272
Min Seo?

349
00:27:54,272 --> 00:27:59,205
Do you want to talk about how hurt you were
when your Dad left home?

350
00:27:59,205 --> 00:28:01,672
Or how he was indifferent
when you were little?

351
00:28:01,672 --> 00:28:03,872
Or any other mistakes he made?

352
00:28:03,872 --> 00:28:07,338
Just tell me everything comfortably.
You can tell me, can't you?

353
00:28:10,672 --> 00:28:12,772
Why aren't you saying anything? Why?

354
00:28:12,772 --> 00:28:15,405
You badmouthed me like that,
but what's so great about that man...

355
00:28:15,405 --> 00:28:17,405
Oh, please!

356
00:28:17,405 --> 00:28:19,672
You two are getting divorced.

357
00:28:20,772 --> 00:28:23,405
So why are you doing this to me?

358
00:28:24,338 --> 00:28:27,372
I thought you were being nicer lately,
but you're still the same.

359
00:29:05,772 --> 00:29:07,372
[I'm here to pick up Min Seo]

360
00:29:07,372 --> 00:29:09,005
[You must be tired, honey. I miss you]

361
00:29:09,005 --> 00:29:13,172
[Could you look into that PI's office
you mentioned before?]

362
00:29:13,172 --> 00:29:16,238
21 Bonggak-dong.

363
00:29:16,238 --> 00:29:19,472
Huh? What's this?

364
00:29:19,472 --> 00:29:21,205
Why isn't it showing up?

365
00:29:23,238 --> 00:29:25,138
Oh, you're here?

366
00:29:27,205 --> 00:29:28,405
That's strange.

367
00:29:28,405 --> 00:29:31,205
21 Bonggak-dong... Why isn't it
showing up on the navigation?

368
00:29:31,205 --> 00:29:32,938
Is it not there?

369
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:37,138
[Please enter the full name, initials,
phone number, or address]

370
00:29:37,138 --> 00:29:40,405
21 Bonggak-dong!

371
00:29:40,405 --> 00:29:43,105
<i>This address no longer exists.</i>

372
00:29:43,105 --> 00:29:46,438
- What?
<i>- Shall I direct you to the previous address?</i>

373
00:29:49,305 --> 00:29:51,838
Yes, navigate.

374
00:29:53,438 --> 00:29:55,038
- Oh, it's showing up.
<i>- Starting navigation.</i>

375
00:29:55,038 --> 00:29:56,772
It's not far from here.

376
00:29:56,772 --> 00:29:58,305
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

377
00:29:58,305 --> 00:30:00,872
- Put on your seat belt.
- Okay.

378
00:30:03,305 --> 00:30:05,872
[21 Bonggak-dong, Yongun City]

379
00:30:08,238 --> 00:30:12,138
[Strongly oppose reckless redevelopment]

380
00:30:12,138 --> 00:30:16,738
[My home value is plummeting,
residents are crying]

381
00:30:24,572 --> 00:30:27,505
<i>I can't be seen in a place like this.</i>

382
00:30:29,272 --> 00:30:32,372
<i>Yeah, I understand.</i>

383
00:30:38,338 --> 00:30:42,238
[T.D.A]

384
00:30:58,072 --> 00:31:00,038
Oh, what brings you here?

385
00:31:00,038 --> 00:31:01,938
Oh, yes, hello.

386
00:31:01,938 --> 00:31:04,672
I was referred here.

387
00:31:07,505 --> 00:31:10,172
Yes, please have a seat
over here for a moment.

388
00:31:20,338 --> 00:31:25,405
[Manager Na Sol, Twin Detective Agency]

389
00:31:34,805 --> 00:31:36,805
Hello.

390
00:31:36,805 --> 00:31:37,805
Yeah.

391
00:31:37,805 --> 00:31:39,972
You called earlier, right?

392
00:31:39,972 --> 00:31:42,038
Oh, yes.

393
00:31:42,038 --> 00:31:44,805
Well, I heard the gist of it.

394
00:31:44,805 --> 00:31:50,072
You're fighting for custody
against your cheating, worthless husband.

395
00:31:51,372 --> 00:31:54,345
You need evidence, but you don't want it

396
00:31:54,345 --> 00:31:56,905
to look like
you hired a private investigator, right?

397
00:31:56,905 --> 00:31:58,072
But, the thing is

398
00:31:58,072 --> 00:32:02,138
privacy laws are pretty strict,
so digging up information isn't easy.

399
00:32:02,138 --> 00:32:06,372
And even if we don't find anything,
you'll still have to pay the fee.

400
00:32:07,138 --> 00:32:10,538
That's why we usually don't take cases
that require this much work.

401
00:32:10,538 --> 00:32:13,438
Huh? Wait a moment.

402
00:32:14,121 --> 00:32:17,493
Crap.

403
00:32:21,138 --> 00:32:23,438
I'm sorry, maybe another time.

404
00:32:24,938 --> 00:32:27,038
Sure, come again if you need anything.

405
00:32:34,372 --> 00:32:36,038
What?

406
00:32:38,572 --> 00:32:40,305
Hold on, hold on!

407
00:32:40,305 --> 00:32:42,272
You should at least hear me out.

408
00:32:42,272 --> 00:32:44,182
- No, it's okay.
- We usually don't take cases

409
00:32:44,182 --> 00:32:45,405
that require this much effort.

410
00:32:45,405 --> 00:32:47,972
But you said your husband
is a real piece of work.

411
00:32:47,972 --> 00:32:49,972
So we'll make an exception for you.

412
00:32:49,972 --> 00:32:52,472
- No.
- I hear there are a lot of

413
00:32:52,472 --> 00:32:56,405
detective agencies these days
that scam their own clients.

414
00:32:56,405 --> 00:32:58,205
It's fine.

415
00:32:58,205 --> 00:33:02,805
Don't end up regretting it after losing
your child to that lousy husband.

416
00:33:10,738 --> 00:33:16,705
Is there a way to make sure I win?

417
00:33:16,705 --> 00:33:19,338
Well, we'll have to find one.

418
00:33:19,338 --> 00:33:25,905
But usually, these things work out.
It'll just cost a little extra.

419
00:33:25,905 --> 00:33:27,505
Yeah.

420
00:33:33,338 --> 00:33:35,638
- Hello.
- Why are you sitting here? You startled me.

421
00:33:35,638 --> 00:33:38,005
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, I have.

422
00:33:38,005 --> 00:33:39,005
[Gogo Used Market, Wang Jae]

423
00:33:39,005 --> 00:33:40,272
[Congrats on your first ad!]

424
00:33:40,272 --> 00:33:42,338
[Thanks, I feel like things have been
going well ever since I met you]

425
00:33:54,705 --> 00:33:57,438
Oh, Director...

426
00:33:58,105 --> 00:34:00,772
about Jae Hong...

427
00:34:00,772 --> 00:34:05,105
I mean, at the clinic, Ryu Ji Su...

428
00:34:06,372 --> 00:34:08,805
Never mind. Have a good day.

429
00:34:08,805 --> 00:34:10,405
Yeah.

430
00:34:25,672 --> 00:34:31,138
[The Day of the Accident]

431
00:34:47,081 --> 00:34:49,572
Let's hurry up and go over there.

432
00:34:49,572 --> 00:34:51,105
- Please come visit us.
- What is this?

433
00:34:51,105 --> 00:34:52,672
Please come visit us. We'll do our best.

434
00:34:52,672 --> 00:34:54,138
- What is this? What is this?
- Thank you.

435
00:34:54,138 --> 00:34:56,972
[24-Hour Unlimited Choice, Unlimited Touch,
Ladies Always Available]

436
00:34:56,972 --> 00:34:58,805
- No, I'm not going. Forget it.
- You're not going?

437
00:34:58,805 --> 00:35:01,505
- We can go if you want.
- Let's just have a drink. What nonsense.

438
00:35:17,005 --> 00:35:18,472
Did you finish it or not?

439
00:35:18,472 --> 00:35:20,772
- You drank it? You did?
- I finished it all, all of it.

440
00:35:20,772 --> 00:35:23,005
Ji Young, you come here too.

441
00:35:23,005 --> 00:35:24,472
No, no...

442
00:35:24,472 --> 00:35:26,005
Huh? What's this?

443
00:35:26,005 --> 00:35:27,805
I'm not used to this kind of thing...

444
00:35:53,705 --> 00:35:57,138
We'll make sure you're comfortable, lawyer.

445
00:35:57,138 --> 00:35:59,005
[Your husband's lawyer
has a lot of dirty tricks]

446
00:35:59,005 --> 00:36:02,172
[I'll see if I can get him on our side]

447
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:09,438
- Huh?
- Director, aren't you heading home?

448
00:36:09,438 --> 00:36:12,038
You can go home.

449
00:36:13,305 --> 00:36:15,738
I'll head out then.

450
00:36:15,738 --> 00:36:17,538
Okay.

451
00:36:34,805 --> 00:36:37,405
Darn it, he's sleeping like a log.

452
00:36:49,638 --> 00:36:51,272
Excuse me.

453
00:36:52,805 --> 00:36:54,472
[Cheongnam Crystal Dermatology]
Excuse me?

454
00:36:56,605 --> 00:36:58,872
What? What if someone sees us?

455
00:36:58,872 --> 00:37:00,772
I sent all the staff home.

456
00:37:00,772 --> 00:37:02,405
Yeah?

457
00:37:04,705 --> 00:37:06,338
Good job.

458
00:37:09,405 --> 00:37:10,772
Mister!

459
00:37:10,772 --> 00:37:13,438
Wake up, okay?

460
00:37:14,272 --> 00:37:19,738
Since you're a lawyer,
I guess I don't need to explain much.

461
00:37:19,738 --> 00:37:21,205
About the minor.

462
00:37:21,205 --> 00:37:24,805
Illegal filming
and even sexual assault. Oh, dear.

463
00:37:24,805 --> 00:37:26,338
She's not a minor, she's not...

464
00:37:26,338 --> 00:37:30,505
- It wasn't sexual assault. No, no, no.
- But, this belongs to you, doesn't it?

465
00:37:30,505 --> 00:37:34,838
The more I looked into this,
the more suspicious things I found.

466
00:37:34,838 --> 00:37:37,872
If I knew it was going to be like this,
I would've just caught you.

467
00:37:37,872 --> 00:37:42,338
Wait, wait, wait...

468
00:37:42,338 --> 00:37:47,209
- Where are you going?
- Hold on, hold on.

469
00:37:50,272 --> 00:37:53,338
Sir, how about this? I'll give you money.

470
00:37:53,338 --> 00:37:54,738
Whatever you want, I'll...

471
00:37:54,738 --> 00:37:56,738
Well, it's worth hundreds
of millions of won, but...

472
00:37:56,738 --> 00:37:58,538
I also have a duty to my client.

473
00:37:58,538 --> 00:38:01,572
- Client? Who's your client?
- That's none of your business.

474
00:38:01,572 --> 00:38:03,772
Well, you know Joo Bo Sung, right?

475
00:38:03,772 --> 00:38:06,605
I heard you've taken on his custody case.

476
00:38:06,605 --> 00:38:09,672
Lose that case cleanly,
and I'll give this back to you.

477
00:38:09,672 --> 00:38:13,805
So, what do you say? Huh?

478
00:38:13,805 --> 00:38:19,005
Anyway, lawyers never give a darn answer.

479
00:38:21,372 --> 00:38:24,038
Sang Cheol! Look here.

480
00:38:24,038 --> 00:38:27,472
There's no CCTV here,
and no one comes around.

481
00:38:27,472 --> 00:38:30,738
I could do whatever I want to you,

482
00:38:30,738 --> 00:38:33,705
and no one would come!

483
00:38:38,872 --> 00:38:42,138
I was actually about to call you.

484
00:38:42,138 --> 00:38:44,438
- We're totally in sync.
- Yeah?

485
00:38:44,438 --> 00:38:47,038
You know the place
you introduced me to last time?

486
00:38:47,038 --> 00:38:50,238
It's a little unusual,
but they seem good at what they do.

487
00:38:50,238 --> 00:38:51,705
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

488
00:38:51,705 --> 00:38:53,005
That's a relief.

489
00:38:53,005 --> 00:38:55,905
I was really struggling because of that.

490
00:38:55,905 --> 00:38:58,272
In return, charge me up now.

491
00:38:58,972 --> 00:39:02,238
Now? Really? Here?

492
00:39:07,638 --> 00:39:08,738
Ta-da!

493
00:39:08,738 --> 00:39:11,872
What? You prepared this too?

494
00:39:11,872 --> 00:39:14,105
This mint one is a bit strong.

495
00:39:14,105 --> 00:39:16,272
So? You don't like it?

496
00:39:16,272 --> 00:39:19,005
No, that's why I like it even more.

497
00:39:26,005 --> 00:39:30,772
Darn it, I'm telling you to listen
while I'm still being nice!

498
00:39:30,772 --> 00:39:32,072
Is it hard to understand?

499
00:39:32,072 --> 00:39:34,338
- I'll lose the case.
- Look at you.

500
00:39:34,338 --> 00:39:36,772
I'll lose the case. I'll lose...

501
00:39:36,772 --> 00:39:39,405
- My phone... I need my phone.
- Your phone?

502
00:39:39,405 --> 00:39:40,705
- I need my phone.
- Fine.

503
00:39:40,705 --> 00:39:44,972
Lose the case, and I'll give your phone back.

504
00:39:51,872 --> 00:39:55,538
You piece of work! You punk! Darn it!

505
